---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getSiteData } from '../lib/baserow';

const data = await getSiteData();
const s = data.settings;
const contactEmail = s.contactEmail || 'info@rootedcommons.uk';
---
<BaseLayout settings={s} pages={data.pages} title="Privacy notice" description="How Roots to Fruits CIC and Rooted Commons use and protect personal information.">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Rooted Commons</p>
      <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="small-print">Last updated: 29 July 2026</p>

      <p>Roots to Fruits CIC, operating the Rooted Commons membership and ordering service, is responsible for the personal information described in this notice. This notice explains what we collect, why we use it, who we share it with, how long we keep it and the choices available to you.</p>

      <h2>Information we collect</h2>
      <p>Depending on how you use Rooted Commons, we may collect your name, email address, phone number, membership status, member reference, weekly commitment, preferred collection day and collection point, newsletter preference, account credit, order history, payment and refund records, communications with us, and technical information needed to operate and secure the website.</p>
      <p>We do not ask you to enter full payment-card details into our website. Where online card payment is offered, the payment provider processes those details under its own privacy notice.</p>

      <h2>How and why we use your information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Membership and orders:</strong> to create and administer your membership, authenticate secure links, accept and prepare orders, allocate collection points, maintain stock records, calculate account credit and contact you about an order. We use this information because it is necessary to provide the membership and ordering service you have requested.</li>
        <li><strong>Payments, accounts and legal records:</strong> to record BACS payments, online payments, refunds, invoices and accounting entries, and to meet tax, company and financial-record obligations. We rely on performance of our agreement with you and compliance with legal obligations.</li>
        <li><strong>Service administration and security:</strong> to prevent duplicate or unauthorised orders, investigate faults, maintain backups and protect the service. We rely on our legitimate interests in operating a reliable and secure community food service.</li>
        <li><strong>News and membership communications:</strong> to send essential service messages about your membership, orders and collections. Where we send optional marketing or promotional emails, we do so with consent or another lawful basis permitted by electronic-marketing law, and you can unsubscribe from those messages.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share information with</h2>
      <p>We use service providers that help us operate Rooted Commons. These may include Baserow for membership, product and order records; Cloudflare and our website-hosting tools for delivery, security and signup abuse prevention (including Turnstile); mailbox.org for email; MailerLite for newsletters and member communications where used; Xero for accounting; and Mollie or another payment provider when online payment is enabled. We disclose only the information reasonably needed for each service.</p>
      <p>We may also share the minimum necessary order or collection information with staff, volunteers, producers and collection-point partners who need it to prepare or hand over your order. We may disclose information where required by law or to establish, exercise or defend legal claims.</p>

      <h2>International processing</h2>
      <p>Some providers may process information outside the United Kingdom. Where this happens, we seek to use providers and contractual safeguards designed to provide an appropriate level of protection, such as UK adequacy regulations or approved contractual clauses.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
      <p>We keep active membership and account records while your membership continues. Order, payment, refund and accounting records are normally retained for up to seven years where needed for financial, tax and audit purposes. Authentication tokens are kept only while required for secure access and may expire or be replaced. Routine enquiries and operational correspondence are deleted when no longer reasonably needed. We may retain limited records for longer where necessary to resolve a dispute or meet a legal requirement.</p>

      <h2>Website storage and cookies</h2>
      <p>The ordering site may use local storage or similar technology to remember your basket, selected collection point and secure member access on your device. These functions are used to provide the service you request. We do not currently use non-essential advertising cookies. If non-essential analytics or marketing technologies are introduced, we will provide appropriate information and choices before using them where consent is required.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances, you may have the right to ask for a copy of your personal information, correct inaccurate information, request deletion or restriction, object to certain uses, and receive information you provided in a portable format. Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw consent at any time without affecting earlier lawful processing.</p>
      <p>To exercise a right or ask a privacy question, email <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>. We may need to confirm your identity before acting on a request.</p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>Please contact us first so we can try to resolve your concern. You also have the right to complain to the UK Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO), the supervisory authority for data protection in the United Kingdom.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>We may update this notice when our services, suppliers or legal obligations change. The latest version will always be published on this page with its revision date.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
